text:
{
  "angles": [
    {
      "angle": "Bitcoin frees people from having to accept government money.",
      "moments": ["863cc95ab7c5e0c11482", "4f9d38e1d86556b36d9c", "8055c5252b61b9639cbe"],
      "hook": "863cc95ab7c5e0c11482",
      "support": {
        "863cc95ab7c5e0c11482": "Hook: 'But in our modern world, we have no choice' creates immediate tension; ends on 'You had to sign up to the government's money,' framing the problem.",
        "4f9d38e1d86556b36d9c": "Follows directly: after 'government's money,' the 'I mean' pivots to confirming Bitcoin's success is independent of the White House, Senate, or House. Ends on persecution making it do well.",
        "8055c5252b61b9639cbe": "After the political-independence point, the 'But' pivots to the full vision: a new internet bound by Bitcoin providing abundance to 8 billion. Closes the arc from problem to solution."
      }
    },
    {
      "angle": "Bitcoin builds its own economic system that no government can control.",
      "moments": ["40ffa6e345a223d30429", "8055c5252b61b9639cbe", "4f9d38e1d86556b36d9c"],
      "hook": "40ffa6e345a223d30429",
      "support": {
        "40ffa6e345a223d30429": "Hook: 'You can have Bitcoin, and money will be created' is a strong declarative opener. Walks through the Bitcoin standard's own credit-creation mechanics, ending on 'denominated in something else.'",
        "8055c5252b61b9639cbe": "After the monetary mechanics, the 'But' zooms out to the broader vision: a new internet bound by Bitcoin, abundance for 8 billion. Natural escalation from 'how it works' to 'what it means.'",
        "4f9d38e1d86556b36d9c": "After the abundance vision, the 'I mean' grounds it in political reality: success doesn't depend on the White House or Congress. Ends on persecution as a tailwind, reinforcing independence."
      }
    },
    {
      "angle": "No one controls Bitcoin's value; it is set by free individual choice and open market forces.",
      "moments": ["3b3050f4afd6f3c011e7", "0c751a33022013fb3086", "01154f025a00f40132a7"],
      "hook": "3b3050f4afd6f3c011e7",
      "support": {
        "3b3050f4afd6f3c011e7": "Hook: 'Bitcoin does not have any authority that allows people to take the wealth of others' is a punchy declarative. Ends on 'they chose to do that,' establishing the free-choice frame.",
        "0c751a33022013fb3086": "After 'they chose to do that,' the 'When' illustrates HOW the market chooses: collective love at the top, hate at the bottom, driving price. Adds the sentiment dimension of free choice.",
        "01154f025a00f40132a7": "After sentiment, the 'Now' adds the macro layer: rates and risk perception shape the free market's verdict. Ends on 'the market definitely sees Bitcoin as risky,' showing the market freely assesses it."
      }
    }
  ]
}
